==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|bʰreg}}
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|refractum}}, the neutral inflection of {{m|la|refractus}}, the past participle of {{m|la|refringere}}, itself from {{m|la|re-||again}} + {{m|la|frangere||to break}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ækt|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|of light}} To change [[direction]] as a result of entering a different [[medium]]
# {{lb|en|transitive|optics}} To cause (light) to change direction as a result of entering a different medium.
#: ''A prism can '''refract''' light.''

